## Storage

Secrets belong only in the deployment provider or GitHub environment secret store. Never place them in source, Markdoc frontmatter, `.env` examples with real values, workflow arguments, issue text, PR comments, screenshots, build artifacts, or test fixtures.

## Required separation

Use separate preview, staging, and production Cloudflare tokens. Each token is limited to the one account and Worker capability needed for its environment. PR workflows cannot read any deployment token. Production secrets are available only after the production environment gate.

## Runtime handling

The Worker reads Turnstile and Resend credentials from bindings. It does not echo them, place them in responses, or log provider response bodies. Audit events contain only event name, request ID, reason category, and status.

## Rotation

Rotate immediately after suspected exposure, staff or vendor access change, unexpected provider activity, or repository history leak. Routine rotation occurs at least every 90 days. Record the rotation time and operator without recording the value.

## Current activation state

The repository defines expected secret names. It does not prove that isolated tokens, environment restrictions, or rotation schedules are configured in GitHub and Cloudflare. The access-review runbook covers that external activation.
